                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8a03b174-7392-3fcf-b5bd-def8330e88b2",
                        "entry_id": "0f5b5f7f-461f-399c-9d8e-a4aa62a1526a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "onbaatzuchtig, niet op eigen voordeel uit zijn"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5b2c4674-5530-4f69-88ff-10c8cbc4bf06",
                                "sense_id": "8a03b174-7392-3fcf-b5bd-def8330e88b2",
                                "text": "Omdat ik merkte dat ik steeds harder begon te praten, stopte ik even en begon koeltjes opnieuw. 'Ze zouden ook blind moeten zijn voor de wetenschap dat mannen zichzelf aanpraten dat mooie vrouwen ook een edelmoedig karakter hebben, hoewel geen enkele lelijke vrouw mooier wordt van welke mate van edelmoedigheid dan ook.'"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c3a6a0c0-de5a-3124-851c-b01cbad0993a",
                        "entry_id": "0f5b5f7f-461f-399c-9d8e-a4aa62a1526a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "vrijgevig met eigen tijd, geld of bezit"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0f5e5373-1103-43e7-9d18-6f21f4878d46",
                        "source_entry_id": "0f5b5f7f-461f-399c-9d8e-a4aa62a1526a",
                        "target_lang_word": "magnanimous",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "magnanimous",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "79b05f58-2c41-35ba-9e06-c6162eb24497",
                                        "entry_id": "65910ba2-c8af-3843-9a70-33d70b0b228c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Noble and generous in spirit."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b05d5e5d-6c29-41d2-b6d0-a53510d0e0e4",
                                                "sense_id": "79b05f58-2c41-35ba-9e06-c6162eb24497",
                                                "text": "She is a theame of honour and renowne, / A ſpurre to valiant and magnanimous deeds, / Whoſe preſent courage may beate downe our foes, / And fame in time to come canonize us, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9703c0fc-0e20-4c1a-a6fc-af7b29051e8e",
                                                "sense_id": "79b05f58-2c41-35ba-9e06-c6162eb24497",
                                                "text": "First, our friendship began at that early time when alone it is unalloyed and sincere; secondly\"—and here, in spite of her vivacity, Marie's voice trembled—\"you are associated with the only being in the world I ever really loved; and thirdly, I have behaved exceedingly ill to you, and, consequently, feel it quite magnanimous not to hate you, which is the established rule on such occasions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c79d1ee7-4a08-424d-8117-fae0a2988b4f",
                                                "sense_id": "79b05f58-2c41-35ba-9e06-c6162eb24497",
                                                "text": "doolittle [sad but magnanimous] They played you off very cunning, Eliza, them two sportsmen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ab40494b-bbe3-48e4-9e08-df4e4d7aa575",
                                                "sense_id": "79b05f58-2c41-35ba-9e06-c6162eb24497",
                                                "text": "I felt vaguely he was a sneak, and remained quite unmollified by advances on his side, which, in a boy's barbarous fashion, unless it suited me to be magnanimous, I haughtily ignored."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a01536c1-65e4-4dfe-ad10-1abef7e9dd63",
                        "source_entry_id": "0f5b5f7f-461f-399c-9d8e-a4aa62a1526a",
                        "target_lang_word": "magnánimo",
                        "target_lang_code": "es",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "magnánimo",
                                "target_lang_code": "es",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8bbf9b5b-c024-3b8e-9829-e4b67c08254c",
                                        "entry_id": "c212df70-a810-3cbf-adb3-a799460adf4a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Que tiene magnanimidad; que posee grandeza de espíritu y actúa noblemente."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ba6026db-603e-458d-9e01-9ef94ebabd77",
                                                "sense_id": "8bbf9b5b-c024-3b8e-9829-e4b67c08254c",
                                                "text": "De magnánimos es llevar con mansedumbre los descuidos."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f01570e1-c2c1-45ce-8238-a6d5c4a6950f",
                                                "sense_id": "8bbf9b5b-c024-3b8e-9829-e4b67c08254c",
                                                "text": "el magnánimo entre todas las acciones virtuosas emprende siempre las mas ilustres y heroicas, á las que ciertamente se deben los primeros honores; y por esto se dice, que la magnanimidad hace grandes todas las otras virtudes."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1d546509-0a0a-3411-8a56-e44c48abe7dd",
                                        "entry_id": "c212df70-a810-3cbf-adb3-a799460adf4a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Que indica o revela magnanimidad."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
